menuconfig MESHTASTIC_EXTNOTIFY
	bool "Meshtastic external notification (board LED)"
	default y
	depends on GPIO
	help
	  The reference ExternalNotificationModule's generic output role: on an
	  incoming text (TEXT_MESSAGE_APP, ALERT_APP, DETECTION_SENSOR_APP) from
	  another node, drive the board's led0 for output_ms, or toggle it every
	  output_ms for nag_timeout seconds; alert_message fires on any
	  non-muted message, alert_bell on one carrying an ASCII BEL (0x07).
	  Driven by ModuleConfig.external_notification, applied live.

	  What this port cannot drive is refused at write time rather than
	  stored and ignored: a raw pin number in `output` (0 = the board LED is
	  the only meaning here), vibra and buzzer outputs and their alert
	  flags, PWM/I2S ringtone playback (set_ringtone is refused too). A
	  board with no led0 alias refuses `enabled`.

if MESHTASTIC_EXTNOTIFY

config MESHTASTIC_EXTNOTIFY_SEED_ENABLED
	bool "First-boot default: enabled"
	default n
	help
	  The reference ships the module enabled on boards that define a
	  notification output. Off here by default: a bench node blinking on
	  every text is a surprise, not a feature. The rest of the seed matches
	  the reference (active-high, alert on message, 1000 ms, 60 s nag).

endif # MESHTASTIC_EXTNOTIFY
